05,0,0,null,1,"6/65/Mus%C3%A9e_Camille_Claudel_08092019_Camille_Claudel_La_Joueuse_de_fl%C3%BBte_8724.jpg/330px-Mus%C3%A9e_Camille_Claudel_08092019_Camille_Claudel_La_Joueuse_de_fl%C3%BBte_8724.jpg",4,6,1,2,7,"La Joueuse de flûte","2010.1.22"],[130014485,"Torso of a Crouching Woman",null,0,0,null,4,"9/97/Torso_of_a_Crouching_Woman%2C_by_Camille_Claudel_%28Getty_109P03%29.jpg/330px-Torso_of_a_Crouching_Woman%2C_by_Camille_Claudel_%28Getty_109P03%29.jpg",4,3,1,0,null,null,null],[134305532,"The Confidence",1893,0,0,null,1,null,null,null,0,0,7,"La Confidence | Les Causeuses | Les Bavardes","2010.1.17"]],"summaryBase":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/","summaryLicence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","summaries":{"3205060":["The Mature Age, also named Destiny, The Path of Life or Fatality (1894–1900) is a sculpture by French artist Camille Claudel. The work was commissioned by the French government in 1895, but the commission was cancelled in 1899 before a bronze was cast.","The Mature Age"],"3376130":["Perseus and the Gorgon is a 1902 monumental sculpture by Camille Claudel that portrays a scene from Greek mythology. The artist sculpted her own likeness for Medusa's face, in anger after the break-up of her romantic partnership with sculptor Auguste Rodin.","Perseus and the Gorgon"],"19945289":["The Waltz or The Waltzers is a sculpture by the French artist Camille Claudel. It depicts two figures, a man and a woman, locked in an amorous embrace as they dance a waltz.","The Waltz (Claudel)"],"31842466":["Sakuntala, also known as Sakountala or Çacountala, is a sculpture by the French artist Camille Claudel, made in several versions in different media from 1886, with a marble version completed in 1905, and bronze castings made from 1905.","Sakuntala (Claudel)"],"67182973":["The Bust of Auguste Rodin was sculpted by the French artist Camille Claudel in 1888-1889 as a tribute to her teacher and lover, Auguste Rodin.","Bust of Auguste Rodin (Claudel)"]},"titlesFrom":["fr","P1476","alias:en","alias:fr","aliasFilter:1"]}